WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.492
Meet Buffer: a read-only way to understand perpetual positions. Start with a

00:00:05.492 --> 00:00:08.492
sample, or read a public Solana account.

00:00:09.392 --> 00:00:15.674
The app opens with SOL, Bitcoin, Ether, and XRP sample positions. Apply

00:00:15.674 --> 00:00:21.957
a ten percent decline. Their contributions combine to positive one thousand USDC.

00:00:21.957 --> 00:00:24.575
These are fixed, illustrative prices.

00:00:25.475 --> 00:00:31.982
Open Add perps and search seventy-six configured sample markets. Add a position,

00:00:31.982 --> 00:00:38.489
change its direction, size, or baseline price. Sample USDC, USDT, and USD

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:41.200
labels do not convert currencies.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:48.293
For public accounts, Velocity is the default. Pacifica also supports price scenarios.

00:00:48.293 --> 00:00:54.485
Jupiter shows position inventory only, with its modeling limits explained. Legacy Drift

00:00:54.485 --> 00:00:56.033
stays clearly paused.

00:00:56.933 --> 00:01:02.351
Inspect each contribution and exclusion, then open Method for the calculation, source,

00:01:02.351 --> 00:01:07.769
and freshness. Save a dated copy on this device, or download the

00:01:07.769 --> 00:01:09.575
exact scenario as JSON.

00:01:10.475 --> 00:01:15.723
Buffer adapts to mobile and desktop. Supported browsers can install it, and

00:01:15.723 --> 00:01:20.971
the public sample calculator works offline. Open Buffer and explore your next

00:01:20.971 --> 00:01:21.408
what-if.
